{
  "@context": {
    "@vocab": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/inklet/finkapp/apps/vocab#"
  },
  "@id": "files",
  "@type": "App",
  "position": 3,
  "id": "files",
  "family": "office",
  "icon": "📁",
  "name": "Files",
  "surface": "window",
  "url": "../apps/files/index.html",
  "desc": "Browse, read and edit your files",
  "wholePod": true,
  "capabilities": [
    "pod:read",
    "pod:write",
    "storage"
  ],
  "silent": true,
  "tools": true,
  "notes": [
    "TOOLS (2026-11-07): list_folder, search and read_file, all read-only, through foafos.tools in app-sdk.js. They read the location Files has open.",
    "wholePod: as the person's file manager, Files is granted the whole pod rather than apps/files/, so it shows what other apps saved. Every other app keeps its own container.",
    "Rebuilt 2026-11-04 as a three-pane explorer over foafos.pod.* (folders, contents, preview), with inklet/apps/ui/panes.css, the layout other complex apps can share. The old edot component in magpie/edot/files is left in place and is no longer launched. It also reached the device (OPFS) mount, which this one does not: the pod verbs are the only storage here.",
    "MIGRATED (July 2026). Files stored nothing itself — its escape hatch was bought for OPFS, which needs an origin to hang a storage bucket on and so is refused outright in a sandboxed frame. It now probes the device mount and falls back to BrokeredResourceSource: the same list/read/write/remove/stat/mkdir interface over the shell's store.",
    "files.html, not the directory: there is no index.html here, so the bare path served a directory listing locally and would 404 on GitHub Pages. The app had never actually loaded inside the shell."
  ]
}
